    {
      "localization": {
        "type": "appStoreVersionLocalizations",
        "id": "eed75cbd-be6c-4585-980f-6bddacab5d22",
        "attributes": {
          "description": "Keep your focus on training.\n\nPowerReps is built for bench press, squat and deadlift. Start on Apple Watch, then review every set on iPhone.\n\nYOUR WHOLE WORKOUT\nStart once and finish with a report of exercises, reps, weights and sets. Change exercises or weight, pause and resume, and review recorded movement time separately from the time between sets.\n\nREVIEW EVERY REP\nExplore rep completion markers, set boundaries and available motion sensor curves on one timeline. Select individual reps, switch sensor channels, and split or merge sets on iPhone.\n\nRECORDS AND TRENDS\nBrowse workouts by date and filter by exercise or date range. Review totals, your training calendar, streaks, exercise distribution and weight history.\n\nLOG, EDIT AND BACK UP\nAdd multi-set workouts, adjust reps and weights, add notes and keep drafts. Export a workout backup, merge records from a backup or share CSV files. Phone edits are preserved when syncing again.\n\nSTART FROM YOUR WATCH\nStart a workout with Siri on Apple Watch and set reminders for days you have not trained. With permission, save workouts to Apple Health and view heart rate and active energy when available. When a count needs correction, confirm the actual reps and choose to send samples as feedback.\n\nAutomatic rep counting requires Apple Watch. iPhone works independently for manual logging and record management. Supports English and Simplified Chinese, with light and dark appearance.",
          "locale": "en-US",
          "keywords": "gym,workout,log,reps,sets,bench press,squat,deadlift,weight,Apple Watch,strength,training,calendar",
          "marketingUrl": null,
          "promotionalText": "Start on your watch. Review on your phone. Whole-workout reports, set timelines and a training calendar keep every session in view.",
          "supportUrl": "https://www.flyingrtx.com",
          "whatsNew": "Updated App Store visuals."
        },
